editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-02.md:33:*Caelen Hesk-ward. 41-7843-V.* He wrote the number slowly, digit by digit, and checked it against the copy of the ruling in the binder, because he had learned that the number you were surest of was the one you were likeliest to get wrong. He wrote *Denvash* and the date. He wrote the designation in brackets, *[SHATTERED]*, as the station had written it, and under it a line saying that the panel at Greyvane had found it did not appear anywhere in the enumerated schedule, with the page of the ruling where it said so. He wrote *Hesk*, and then, because Bracken had asked how it was spelled, he wrote it again in capitals, and then felt foolish, and left it.
