Out of this recheck's scope; spanning movements or belonging to the ledger.

- **Ledger end-state for M8 / Book 3.** Needs writing: the calendar (ruling Tuesday wk22; remand entered wk22; Lira's release Monday wk23; Ember resumed Thursday wk23; D7 Tuesday wk24; Hesk's letter Wednesday wk24; the boxes Wednesday–Friday wk24; the gap left on the shelf); Cael's body (the burn a closed scar; the pivot a tenth late); the finding that Ember costs the same at any size ("a letting-go," the second of three rewordings; "decision point" reserved for B4 ch21); the record exposure (ruling public; transcript requested by registry offices; the faceless cover); who knows what.
- **New canon minted in r1, for the ledger.** Cael promised Vell he would write ("I said I'd write"); Vell "taught him to read a ledger … every line, in order" — Book 2's edition is undrafted and can plant both. Havel was trained by an old recorder (a woman, forty years at desks) who taught him to read a room by its coughs and to warm ink for a count of twenty; this sits beside M7's "Assessor Havel … Recording officer now … a new grade," and the ledger should say which came first. Greyvane "was a waystation for longer than it's been a school" (Quenna), consistent with ch54's "old waystation" and M7's four-hundred-year house. Recorders mark silences with dashes; "there was no mark for an absence."
- **Hand-off facts no longer restated in M8.** Lira's P8 flag and Brom's P9 wall were restated only in Quenna's cut list and the cut wall recap; they are planted in ch10 and now rest on the ledger alone. Book 4 ch1 (the flag transfers) and ch3 ("Wray told me there was a wall") depend on them; the end-state ledger should list both as open.
- **Residual source shadow, pre-repair text, not in the brief.** ch61 s4, Edran: "He went back to his count before Cael could find an answer, which Cael suspected was the point" (0.48) and the "costs nothing to give and a great deal to get out" turn (0.36). ch61 s5, the wall's connective beats (Karis first; "take the argument"; the binder on the knee; brass then slate), which the packet dictates in order. ch54 s3 (29% close) and ch55 s3 (29%) were not flagged by the editorial review; ch55 s3 is the deposition read aloud (fixed content); ch54 s3 is the second room-portrait, worth one spot-check. ch60 s4 (35%) is the archive scene's packet lines ("most famous clerical error," "under his desk," "It's jurisdictional").
- **A small pre-existing doubling.** The term's count (ch61) has Lira, having read the Wind page, "says I'm a tenth late on the second figure," the same words Wray says at D7 three paragraphs earlier. If Lira is agreeing with Wray it is fine; if it should be her own observation, one of the two wants a different figure.
- **Book-level sums.** POV by word count (Cael about 78.5% of M8; cutaways about 8,070 against about 10,000) for the planner's book total. Progression vocabulary far under plan across M7–M8 (the system is the code; reported, not forced). Length: the book's total against its band after M8 lost ~1,400 words.
- **Carried from M7's ledger.** Book 4 bible-pass flags: B4 ch18 "of the preceding year"; B4 "in the second hour of a review" against the three-day courier.
- **Housekeeping.** The movement's `metrics.txt`, `source-overlap.summary` and `AUTHORSHIP.md` predate r1 and should be regenerated or annotated at close.
