+
+Speaker attribution and referents are clean across the seven chapters. Multi-person scenes establish the speaker before alternation, the fight score and eight exchanges remain trackable, and the transition between chapters 1 and 2 now tells a younger listener why the chronology steps back from week fourteen to week eleven. The week-twelve false alarm makes the legal search a changing problem rather than another summary of the same proof. Quenna and Prynn's farewells now trust their gestures sooner, and chapter 7 preserves the distinction among Karis's institutional inference, Withrow's personal conviction, and Cael's unresolved judgment without saying the answer three times.
